{#
  The end of every page's Markdown (TASK-346): a heading, then link lists.

  `byline` is a post's author, a `label` and the `url` of their archive.
  `navigation` is every item of every menu the site stores, each URL once,
  each a `label` and a `url`; `menus` has them by menu name, as the HTML
  does. `home`, `previous` and `next` are here too, though the
  front matter already carries them for a Markdown browser.

  Each link is a line of its own, with its own words, so the same data can be
  written as a Gemini link line. Nothing is printed when there is nothing to
  link.
#}
{% if byline or navigation.length %}
## {{ site.title | escapeMarkdown }}

{% if byline %}
[Written by {{ byline.label | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ byline.url | markdownUrl }})

{% endif %}
{% for item in navigation %}
- [{{ item.label | escapeMarkdown }}]({{ item.url | markdownUrl }})
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
